# Per-package statement-coverage floors, enforced by `make cover`. Reviewed like code.
#
# Floors ratchet upward only. `make cover-ratchet` raises a floor once measured coverage clears
# it by a whole point; nothing lowers one. A pull request that lowers a floor fails
# `make cover-ratchet-check` unless a commit on the branch carries an anchored
# `coverage-floor-lowered: <package> <reason>` line naming the lowered package.
#
# A floored package that exists but declares no functions yet reports PENDING and passes. Once
# it has code, a missing profile entry is a failure: deleting a package's tests must not
# silently satisfy its floor. PLAN.md section 11 wants no vanity global number, so a package
# earns a line here when its semantics are worth a number.
#
# package                          floor%  note
internal/queue                     90.0    PLAN.md section 11: the pure state machine
internal/store                     85.0    PLAN.md section 11: durability and recovery
internal/subject                   95.0    issue #3: a matcher bug misroutes silently
internal/id                        95.0    issue #3: ids are the spine of messq trace
internal/errs                      95.0    issue #3: the closed sentinel set
internal/clock                     90.0    issue #3: the seam every timing test runs through
internal/lifecycle                 90.0    issue #17: the daemon state machine and stop ordering
internal/auth                      90.0    issue #16: the pure security core (pattern, roles, verify, preflight)
internal/docsguard                 95.0    issue #4: the gate that keeps the normative spec honest
internal/testutil/ledger           85.0    issue #8: the three-valued reconciliation ledger oracle
internal/wirecheck                 90.0    issue #18: canonical JSON, normaliser, digests, classifier
internal/wirecode                  95.0    issue #18: the closed machine-code enum source
internal/obs                       90.0    issue #19: the closed vocabulary is the three-surface contract
internal/cli/flagx                 95.0    issue #24: one parser per concept, shared by every command flag
internal/cli/exit                  95.0    issue #23: the exit-code contract is a pure table
internal/cli/conf                  95.0    issue #23: three-layer resolution is a pure precedence engine
internal/cli/render                90.0    issue #23: the output contract and its sanitiser
internal/cli/exec                  90.0    issue #25: exec pure core (words/reason/outcome/env) and child safety
internal/cli/uierr                 90.0    issue #23: teaching errors and the no-invented-text rule
internal/cli                       70.0    issue #24: the View contract and command faces; raised as bodies land
internal/janitor                   85.0    issue #27: housekeeping bounds and the disk-safety state machine
internal/ops/backup                70.0    issue #30: the VACUUM INTO snapshot pipeline
internal/doctor                    70.0    issue #30: pure checks over a collected snapshot
